  "published": "2026-10-16T22:06:45.91Z",
  "releaseNotes": "## v4.4.2 - One-line deletes (DeleteDataAsync, DeleteObjectAsync, DeleteAllDataAsync, DeleteAllObjectsAsync), safe straight after a restart; the API remembers the hApp it was initialised with, so one-line calls keep using it after ShutdownAsync / restarts.\n\n## v4.4.1 - The bundled oasis.happ now has the HyperNET zome functions, so SendSignalAsync works with the default hApp (the previous bundled build predated them).\n\n## v4.4.0 - Direct messages: SendSignalAsync + OnSignalReceived (remote signals, peer to peer); ReceiveSignal returns the last message (SendSignal/ReceiveSignal were placeholders); XML docs for every member.\n\n## v4.2.0 - first release on NuGet; works against the Holochain 0.7 OASIS hApp (0.7.0 and 0.7.1)\n\n- Simple key/value + object store: SaveDataAsync/LoadDataAsync, SaveObjectAsync/LoadObjectAsync<T>, one hApp entry per StoreId, created then updated by action hash.\n- Reuses the installed app (data survives restarts); errors reported through OnError, LastError and each result's Message; ShutdownAsync.\n- New HoloNETAPIHapp overloads; the old (hAppId, hAppPath, hAppRole) string overloads are obsolete because they could bind to the zome/function overloads.\n- Fully tested against real Holochain 0.7.0 and 0.7.1 conductors (1,758 + 9 live/fake-conductor tests on each), line coverage ~93%.\n- Requires NextGenSoftware.Logging / NextGenSoftware.WebSocket 2.0.4 (fixes below).\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/holochain-open-dev/holochain-client-csharp/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\n\n---\n\nInitial public release of HoloNET API.",
